    title: 'Best Places to See Leopards in India: Jhalana, Jawai & More',
    description: 'The best place to see a leopard in India: Jhalana and Jawai in Rajasthan lead, then Tadoba, Satpura, Kabini and Pench. Seasons, odds and how to plan.',
    h1: 'Best Places to See Leopards in India', breadcrumb: 'Best Places to See Leopards', eyebrow: 'Leopard safari guide · 2026–27',
    hero: 'home_images/indian-leopard-wildlife-05.webp', heroAlt: 'Indian leopard looking out from a rocky outcrop',
    commercial: false, schemaType: 'Article', published: '2026-10-17',
    authors: [HARDIK], bylineNote: 'Built from leopard safaris we plan in Rajasthan and Central India.',
    intro: 'The best places to see leopards in India are Jhalana in Jaipur and Jawai-Bera in Rajasthan, where leopards are the main attraction and sightings are frequent. India has an estimated 13,874 leopards (2022), most in Madhya Pradesh. Inside tiger reserves, Tadoba’s buffer, Satpura, Kabini and Pench give good chances.',
